# Smoke Coverage Audit — Part 5: Compile Error Candidates & Methodology

File: openOODA/audit/smoke_coverage_audit_part5.oot
Logline: Catalogs compile failure candidates, formal proof exclusions, surviving import stubs, and classification methodology.

Setup: Details known module compilation risks and test fixture categorization methodology.

Beats:
  1. Likely compile failures and name-drift modules across crypto, math, and wasm.
  2. Product proof (5,888) and verifier (397) exclusions.
  3. Surviving 30 adversarial import stubs for first easy wins.
  4. Appendix B: Methodology notes and audit limitations.

================================================================
BEAT 6 — COMPILE-ERROR CANDIDATES
================================================================

The following modules are likely to fail the smoke test not because
the test is wrong but because the module does not compile, has
missing exports, or has been renamed. Wave 2 workers should expect
these and triage them first (file a missing-export or rename
follow-up instead of writing a test that "passes" against a
different module).

6.1  Likely compile failures (by observation of file content)
      std/crypto/fhe*.oo              Many `fhe_*` modules import
                                      runtime symbols that may
                                      not exist outside the
                                      product C runtime.
      std/crypto/kyber.oo             NTT/INTT helpers may be
                                      under a renamed export.
      std/crypto/pqc_nist/fips205_*.oo       SLH-DSA address scheme has
                                      moved twice; name drift
                                      is likely.
      std/math/bigdecimal*.oo         Mixed-mode arithmetic on
                                      fixed-point may not type-
                                      check against the current
                                      `Int` runtime.
      std/math/matrix_inversion.oo    Inverse may require
                                      `gauss_jordan_*` helpers
                                      not yet exported.
      std/ui/3d/gaussian_*.oo            The "gaussian" stack is
                                      partially stubbed; the
                                      stubs/tags split means
                                      types in `gaussian_types.oo`
                                      and ops in
                                      `gaussian_ops.oo` may not
                                      line up.
      std/compile/wasm_interpreter/wasm_*.oo  194 modules — expect
                                      at least 10–20 to have
                                      stale type names.
      std/formal_proofs/prove_*.oo    5,888 files — most are
                                      product proofs and do
                                      NOT need a smoke test;
                                      treat them as opt-in.
      std/proof_verifiers/*.oo        397 files — most are
                                      verify_*-style fixtures
                                      already exercised by the
                                      smoke harness; do NOT add
                                      redundant *_smoke.oo
                                      fixtures for them.
      std/hw/arch_aarch64/*.oo           128 files — backend code,
                                      tested via the aarch64
                                      ELF smoke path, not
                                      fixtures/*_smoke.oo.
      std/hw/arch_x86/*.oo               100 files — same as aarch64.
      std/test.oo, std/_template.oo   scaffolding; do not test.
      std/byte.oo, str.oo, option.oo
      std/result.oo, macro.oo, math.oo, sh.oo, scenario.oo, semver.oo
                                      tiny core primitives —
                                      already exercised by every
                                      existing smoke fixture;
                                      do not test.

6.2  Modules in std/formal_proofs/ (5,888) and std/proof_verifiers/
     (397) are EXCLUDED from the Wave 2 top-priority list. The
     formal_proofs files are auto-generated "product proof"
     functions (one verify_prove_prod_<topic>() per imported target
     module); they are not first-class APIs. The proof_verifiers
     files are the "verify_*" in-tree deterministic tests already
     exercised by the smoke harness. Neither category needs a new
     fixtures/*_smoke.oo file. If a real test is desired for one of
     these, write it against the *underlying* module in its own
     std/ subtree (e.g., write a smoke for std/av/f16.oo, not for
     std/formal_proofs/prove_prod_a0_f16.oo).

6.3  The 30 second-generation "adversarial import" stubs that
     survived the cleanup. Each is a fixtures/*_smoke.oo that
     just imports a std/ module and prints "OK". They verify the
     module compiles but assert nothing about its behaviour.
     Wave 2 subagents should consider upgrading one of these in
     place (replace the stub body with real assertions) rather
     than writing a brand-new fixture from scratch — the
     boilerplate is already on disk:

         sec/cps/dnp3_types.oo              sec/cps/do178c_types.oo
         sec/cps/esd_types.oo               sec/cps/goose_sec_types.oo
         sec/cps/modbus_sec_types.oo        sec/cps/secoc_types.oo
         sec/cps/sil_types.oo               sec/cps/sis_types.oo
         hash/sha3_round.oo                 hash/sha3_state.oo
         hash/sha3_state_set.oo             hash/sha512_arith.oo
         hash/sha512_compress.oo            hash/sha512_sigma.oo
         enterprise/auth_mfa.oo             enterprise/auth_policy.oo
         enterprise/compliance_evidence.oo  enterprise/erp_types.oo
         formats/arrow_types.oo             formats/flatbuffers_types.oo
         finance/orderbook_types.oo         robot/ros_msg.oo
         robotics/ekf_types.oo              typestate_protocols/typestate_lib.oo
         arch_aarch64/aarch64_empty.oo      arch_aarch64/aarch64_nomain.oo
         arch_x86/x86_empty.oo              wasm_interpreter/wasm_empty.oo
         wasm_interpreter/wasm_nofn.oo      _template.oo

     These 30 modules correspond to category COVERED_BY_IMPORT_STUB
     in part 2 and are recommended for the "first easy wins" track
     (low effort, high residual payoff, one fixtures/*_smoke.oo
     already on disk).

================================================================
APPENDIX B — METHODOLOGY NOTES
================================================================

B.1  How a fixture was classified
      A fixture was classified as REAL if it had at least one of
      the following markers: expect_eq / expect_true / expect_false
      helper, a `FAIL <label>` line, an explicit `process_exit(1)`
      on assertion failure, or a comparison against a known
      constant that is not just "0". This filter retained exactly
      20 of 12,507 fixtures; the rest were classified as STUB.
      Stubs use the "VALID + NEGATIVE TRUST + ADVERSARIAL +
      DOUBLE-RUN" boilerplate and call a marker function
      (shim_marker_identity, <module>_<topic>_marker,
      verify_<module>, init_<module>_cfg, etc.) four times before
      printing "OK".

B.2  How the audit is robust to the in-flight cleanup
      The audit only depends on the 20 REAL fixtures, which the
      cleanup preserves. The 12,487 STUB fixtures are not
      referenced; once they are deleted, every previously-stub
      module simply joins the UNCOVERED set. The category counts
      in 1.1 and part 2/3 do not change as the cleanup progresses.

B.3  Limitations
      * Module API inspection was done by `head -50` of selected
        files; the test-kind column in part 3/4 is the auditor's best
        guess based on the file's "Logline" header. Subagents
        should re-verify the public surface via `ooda reflect`
        before writing a test.
      * Some modules in std/ui/3d/, std/ai/, std/ai/ml_lib/, std/bio/,
        std/econ/fin/, std/phys/quantum/ are stubs themselves (suffix
        `_stubs.oo`, `_types.oo`, `_ops.oo`, `_engine.oo`) —
        the test should target the orchestrator module
        (e.g. std/ui/3d/mesh.oo, not std/ui/3d/mesh_stubs.oo).
      * 434 files end in `_stubs.oo` or `_tags.oo`; these are
        scaffolding and should not be smoke-tested.
